# Luminary marker — cli#254 sub-step 1 (real smoke-expect.sh)
- date: 2026-09-26
- branch: feat/254-smoke-expect-real-body
- parent-pr: #255 (walking skeleton — Cockburn lead)
- lead: john-ousterhout
- supporting: [kent-beck, michael-feathers]
- rationale:
  - lead (Ousterhout) — smoke-expect.sh IS a deep module. Callers stay
    in bash and get 5 verbs. Behind those verbs sits expect(1)'s Tcl
    syntax, escape rules, buffer semantics, and subprocess lifetime.
    Real bodies must keep the narrow interface stable while the
    implementation hides every Tcl quirk. Ousterhout's deep-module
    lens verifies the ship at Step 5.5.
  - supporting (Beck) — RED-first TDD. Each verb ships with failing
    tests first, then bodies. No source landing without a red test
    that the body turns green.
  - supporting (Feathers) — characterization tests. Pin the actual
    behavior against a real expect fixture (fake claude that echoes)
    before naming the fix. Tests grow into a safety net for the drive
    cures in sub-steps 2-4.
- balancing-check-role: lead (Ousterhout) confirms all findings cleared
  before Step 6 merge per loop-discipline.md 5.5.
- ship-form-verified: [ ] pending — set at Step 5.5.
